; AmigaCLISP: run once from the AmigaCLISP folder: Execute Install
; Assigns CLISP: here (now and in S:User-Startup) and saves the memory image.
Assign CLISP: ""
Protect CLISP:CLISP +s QUIET
Set clispdir "`CD`"
Search S:User-Startup "Assign CLISP:" QUIET >NIL:
If WARN
  Echo "Assign CLISP: *"$clispdir*"" >>S:User-Startup
  Echo "Install: added Assign CLISP: to S:User-Startup"
EndIf
UnSet clispdir
Execute CLISP:MakeImage
Echo "Install: done. Start CLISP with CLISP:CLISP"
